        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle - e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},3 e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(- e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(3 e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{(3\\cos(t)-1\\sin(t))^2+(3\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t))^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{9\\cos(t)^2-6\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\sin(t)^2+9\\sin(t)^2+6\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t)^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{10(\\cos^2(t)+\\sin^2(t))} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10} \\int_{0}^{1}e^{3 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}}{3}\\big|_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}\\left(e^{3}-1\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
