        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=\\langle 4 t + 2,- \\frac{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{2 t + 1}\\rangle$ from $t=0$ to $t=1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186119744/plots/curve-e43fb34976ea07bdde3630b4.png)",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(4 t + 2),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- \\frac{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{2 t + 1})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle 4,- 2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(4)^2+(- 2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}})^2} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{4+\\left(\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^2}-(2 t + 1)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^4}-2+(2 t + 1)^4} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^4}+2+(2 t + 1)^4} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^2}+(2 t + 1)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $2 t + 1>0$ throughout the given interval.\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2 t + 1$, $\\mathrm{d}u=2\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}u^{2} + \\frac{1}{u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{u^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{u}\\big|_{1}^{3} \\\\ &=1\\left[\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{3^3}{3}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{1^3}{3}\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{28}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
